      "writtenOn": "2023-06-08T10:38:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, these are push metrics. The idea is that we are just concerned about collecting 24 hours worth of data. The time of upload itself does not need to be uniform. \n\nOn the contrary, if we pulled at the same time, that would probably skew things since some devices would have been tracking data with less than 24 hours and durations won\u0027t add to 24 hours.",
      "parentUuid": "acf01270_3eb1147c",
      "revId": "d8d8f02f4fc28135abc69432466af781a8ba25bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70775e8a_1bb1d57f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-09T06:16:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The time of upload is irrelevant ; this is just pushing the data to statsd, which uploads them whenever it wants.\n\nIf we always push at the same time obviously we\u0027d only do this after we\u0027d have 24h of data the first time (so we\u0027d drop the first batch).\n\nThis makes me think that to avoid skewing the data, we might need to select a random second in the day to push, and drop the data at first alarm (because it doesn\u0027t have 24h, as you pointed out)",
      "parentUuid": "db1c711b_71457c3b",
      "revId": "d8d8f02f4fc28135abc69432466af781a8ba25bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
